---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
const email = 'hello@lifeatthefrontier.com';
---
<LegalPage
  heading="Terms"
  path="/terms"
  updated="25 November 2026"
  description="The terms for using the Life at the Frontier website, podcast and newsletter, including why nothing we publish is financial, medical or legal advice."
>
  <p class="lf-doc-lead">
    These terms apply to lifeatthefrontier.com and to the Life at the Frontier podcast and newsletter,
    created and hosted by Mehdi Nayebi ("we", "us"). By using the site or our content, you agree to
    them. If you do not agree, please do not use them.
  </p>

  <h2>Not advice</h2>
  <p>
    Life at the Frontier explores science, technology and the businesses built on them. Everything we
    publish is for information and discussion only. It is not financial, investment, legal, medical
    or any other professional advice, and it is not a recommendation to buy or sell any security or to
    make any decision.
  </p>
  <p>
    Frontier technologies are uncertain by nature. Forecasts can be wrong, companies can fail, and
    investments can lose value. Do your own research and speak to a qualified professional before you
    act on anything you hear or read here.
  </p>

  <h2>Guests and their views</h2>
  <p>
    Guests speak for themselves. Their views are not necessarily ours, and appearing on the show is not
    an endorsement of a guest, their company or their products. Guests or the host may have interests
    in the subjects discussed. We disclose relevant interests as set out in our
    <a href="/editorial-standards">editorial standards</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to get things right, but we cannot promise that everything we publish is complete,
    accurate or up to date, and fields at the frontier move quickly. When we find a mistake we correct
    it. If you spot one, please tell us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The Life at the Frontier name, logo, website, podcast episodes, newsletter and other materials
    belong to us or to the people who licensed them to us. You are welcome to listen, read, and share
    links to our content, and to quote short extracts with credit to Life at the Frontier and a link back.
  </p>
  <p>
    Please do not copy, republish, sell or adapt our content, or use our name or logo, without written
    permission. You may not use our content to train artificial intelligence models, or to create
    synthetic versions of the host's or guests' voices or likenesses.
  </p>

  <h2>The newsletter</h2>
  <p>
    The newsletter is free. You can unsubscribe at any time with the link in every email. We may change
    or stop the newsletter at any time. How we handle your email address is explained in our
    <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other services</h2>
  <p>
    Our site and content link to other websites and to the platforms where the podcast is available.
    We do not control them and are not responsible for their content or practices. Their own terms and
    privacy policies apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>
    Please do not misuse the site: do not try to break or overload it, gain unauthorised access to it,
    or use it for anything unlawful. We may change, suspend or withdraw the site or any content at any
    time.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The site and our content are provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. To the fullest extent
    the law allows, we are not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of, or reliance on,
    the site or our content. Nothing in these terms limits any liability that cannot be limited by law,
    or takes away your rights as a consumer.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top shows when they last changed. If
    you keep using the site after a change, the updated terms apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
